 your images. Fast. Optimized. Easy to use.</div></div><div class="lg:grid-cols-2 relative lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-flow-row-dense lg:gap-8 lg:items-center"><div class="relative"><h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl text-gray-900">Efficient packing algorithms</h3><dl class="mt-10 space-y-10"><div class="relative ml-16"><dt class="text-lg leading-6 font-medium text-gray-900"><div class="absolute -left-16 top-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-center rounded-md h-12 w-12 bg-linear-to-br from-texturepacker-500 to-texturepacker-700 text-white"><svg viewBox="0 0 23 23" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" stroke="currentColor" fill="none" stroke-width="0.75" role="img" aria-hidden="true" class="h-10 w-10">        <path d="M.5.5h4v6h-4zM.5 8.5h4v6h-4zM.5 16.5h4v6h-4zM6.5.5h4v6h-4zM6.5 8.5h4v6h-4zM6.5 16.5h4v6h-4zM12.5.5h4v6h-4zM12.5 8.5h4v6h-4zM12.5 16.5h4v6h-4zM18.5.5h4v6h-4zM18.5 8.5h4v6h-4zM18.5 16.5h4v6h-4z"></path></svg></div></div>Grid</dt><dd class="mt-2 text-base prose text-gray-600">Use this algorithm if your game engine doesn&#x27;t support sheet data files. All sprites are packed in an equal spaced grid.</dd></div><div class="relative ml-16"><dt class="text-lg leading-6 font-medium text-gray-900"><div class="absolute -left-16 top-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-center rounded-md h-12 w-12 bg-linear-to-br from-texturepacker-500 to-texturepacker-700 text-white"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" stroke-width="0.75" role="img" aria-hidden="true" class="h-10 w-10">    <path fill="none" stroke="currentColor" d="M1.5 1.5h6v5h-6zM9.5 1.5h6v3h-6zM17 1.5h6V7h-6zM1.5 8.5h6v5h-6zM9.5 8.5h4V12h-4zM15.5 8.5H19v5h-3.5zM20.25 8.5H23v3h-2.75zM1.5 15.5h3v3h-3zM6.5 15.5h3v3h-3zM11.5 15.5h3v3h-3zM16.5 15.5h6v3h-6zM1.5 20.5h3v2h-3zM6.5 20.5h3v2h-3zM11.5 20.5h2v2h-2zM15.5 20.5h2v2h-2zM19.5 20.5h2v2h-2z"></path></svg></div></div>Basic</dt><dd class="mt-2 text-base prose text-gray-600">The basic algorithm fills the sprite sheet from top to bottom, different sprite sizes are supported. It&#x27;s the fastest algorithm but usually requires more space.</dd></div><div class="relative ml-16"><dt class="text-lg leading-6 font-medium text-gray-900"><div class="absolute -left-16 top-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-center rounded-md h-12 w-12 bg-linear-to-br from-texturepacker-500 to-texturepacker-700 text-white"><svg viewBox="0 0 23 23" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.75" role="img" aria-hidden="true" class="h-10 w-10">        <path d="M.5.5h4v6h-4zM6.5.5h4v2h-4zM12.5.5h4v2h-4zM18.5.5h4v2h-4zM12.5 4.5h4v4h-4zM12.5 14.5h3v2h-3zM12.5 10.5h5v2h-5zM12.5 18.5h4v3h-4zM18.5 4.5h4v3h-4zM19.5 9.5h3v3h-3zM17.5 14.5h5v2h-5zM18.5 18.5h4v3h-4zM6.5 4.5h4v2h-4zM.5 8.5h4v5h-4zM6.5 8.5h4v5h-4zM6.5 15.5h4v2h-4zM6.5 19.5h4v2h-4zM.5 15.5h4v6h-4z"></path></svg></div></div>MaxRects</dt><dd class="mt-2 text-base prose text-gray-600">This algorithm minimizes the sprite sheet size by placing sprites in gaps between other sprites. Your game engine must be able to import packing information files — which most game engines do.</dd></div><div class="relative ml-16"><dt class="text-lg leading-6 font-medium text-gray-900"><div class="absolute -left-16 top-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-center rounded-md h-12 w-12 bg-linear-to-br from-texturepacker-500 to-texturepacker-700 text-white"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.75" role="img" aria-hidden="true" class="h-10 w-10">    <path d="M17.5 1.5h-16v9h4v-7h8v5l4-2v-5z M7.5 5.5h4v5h-4zM14.596 15.232l-2.828-2.828-6.364 6.364 2.828 2.828 6.364-6.364zM1.5 20.5l8-8h-5l-3 3v5zM15.5 17.5h7v-5l-3 2.5H18l-2.5 2.5zM19.5 12.5l3-2v-5l-3 2v5zM19.583 5.583L22.5 3.5v-2h-3l.083 4.083zM14.5 12.417l2 2.083 1-2.083h-3zM13.5 10.417l4 .083v-2l-4 1.917zM1.5 12.5v1l1-1h-1zM18.5 22.417l4 .083v-3l-4 2.917zM19.5 19.5h-4v3l4-3zM1.5 22.417l5 .083-2-2-3 1.917zM9.5 22.5l3.982.018.018-4.018-4 4z"></path></svg></div></div>Polygon</dt><dd class="mt-2 text-base prose text-gray-600">The polygon algorithm removes transparent parts of the sprites to pack them even tighter. This requires a game engine that supports polygon sprites. E.g. Unity or cocos2d-x.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="mt-10 -mx-4 relative lg:mt-0" aria-hidden="true"><div class="z-10"><figure><div class="bg-texturepacker-400 border border-gray-900 shadow-md"><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper="" class="gatsby-image-wrapper gatsby-image-wrapper-constrained"><div style="max-width:2048px;display:block"><img alt="" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" src="data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg%20height=&#x27;1152&#x27;%20width=&#x27;2048&#x27;%20xmlns=&#x27;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#x27;%20version=&#x27;1.1&#x27;%3E%3C/svg%3E" style="max-width:100%;display:block;position:static"/></div><div aria-hidden="true" data-placeholder-image="" style="opacity:1;transition:opacity 500ms linear;background-color:#886848;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0"></div><picture><source type="image/webp" data-srcset="/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/5d10f/kenney-sheet.webp 512w,/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/30a1f/kenney-sheet.webp 1024w,/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/d9980/kenney-sheet.webp 2048w" sizes="(min-width: 2048px) 2048px, 100vw"/><img data-gatsby-image-ssr="" data-main-image="" style="opacity:0" sizes="(min-width: 2048px) 2048px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" data-src="/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/5e92a/kenney-sheet.png" data-srcset="/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/37319/kenney-sheet.png 512w,/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/011c1/kenney-sheet.png 1024w,/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/5e92a/kenney-sheet.png 2048w" alt="Polygon packed sprites on a sprite sheet"/></picture><noscript><picture><source type="image/webp" srcSet="/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/5d10f/kenney-sheet.webp 512w,/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/30a1f/kenney-sheet.webp 1024w,/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/d9980/kenney-sheet.webp 2048w" sizes="(min-width: 2048px) 2048px, 100vw"/><img data-gatsby-image-ssr="" data-main-image="" style="opacity:0" sizes="(min-width: 2048px) 2048px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/5e92a/kenney-sheet.png" srcSet="/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/37319/kenney-sheet.png 512w,/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/011c1/kenney-sheet.png 1024w,/static/6e83a0415df1372b64e7b30d36b63450/5e92a/kenney-sheet.png 2048w" alt="Polygon packed sprites on a sprite sheet"/></picture></noscript><script type="module">const t="undefined"!=typeof HTMLImageElement&&"loading"in HTMLImageElement.prototype;if(t){const t=document.querySelectorAll("img[data-main-image]");for(let e of t){e.dataset.src&&(e.setAttribute("src",e.dataset.src),e.removeAttribute("data-src")),e.dataset.srcset&&(e.setAttribute("srcset",e.dataset.srcset),e.removeAttribute("data-srcset"));const t=e.parentNode.querySelectorAll("source[data-srcset]");for(let e of t)e.setAttribute("srcset",e.dataset.srcset),e.removeAttribute("data-srcset");e.complete&&(e.style.opacity=1,e.parentNode.parentNode.querySelector("[data-placeholder-image]").style.opacity=0)}}</script></div></div><figcaption class="text-center text-sm text-gray-700 py-1">Sprite sheet packed with TexturePacker&#x27;s polygon algorithm.</figcaption></figure></div></div></div><div class="lg:grid-cols-2 relative lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-flow-row-dense lg:gap-8 lg:items-center"><div class="relative lg:col-start-2"><h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl text-gray-900">Trimming and identical sprite detection</h3><dl class="mt-10 space-y-10"><div class="relative ml-16"><dt class="text-lg leading-6 font-medium text-gray-900"><div class="absolute -left-16 top-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-center rounded-md h-12 w-12 bg-linear-to-br from-texturepacker-500 to-texturepacker-700 text-white"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 512 512" fill="currentColor" role="img" aria-hidden="true" class="h-6 w-6"><path d="M488 320h-72V118.62l93.66-93.66c3.12-3.12 3.12-8.19 0-11.31L498.35 2.34c-3.12-3.12-8.19-3.12-11.31 0L393.37 96H192V24c0-13.26-10.75-24-24-24h-48c-13.25 0-24 10.74-24 24v72H24c-13.25 0-24 10.74-24 24v48c0 13.25 10.75 24 24 24h72v192c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h192v72c0 13.25 10.75 24 24 24h48c13.25 0 24-10.75 24-24v-72h72c13.25 0 24-10.75 24-24v-48c0-13.25-10.75-24-24-24zM96 160H32v-32h64v32zm96-32h169.37l-32 32H192v-32zm105.38 64L192 297.38V192h105.38zM320 384H128V32h32v320h160v32zm-105.38-64L320 214.63V320H214.62zM352 480V182.63l32-32V480h-32zm128-96h-64v-32h64v32z"></path></svg></div></div>Trimming / Crop</dt><dd class="mt-2 text-base prose text-gray-600">Trimming removes transparent areas around a sprite which allows tighter placement of the sprites. This decreases the memory usage and at the same time increases the performance of your game. A data file contains the information about the trimmed areas — this is why the sprites still behave in the same way as the original sprites in your game engine.</dd></div><div class="relative ml-16"><dt class="text-lg leading-6 font-medium text-gray-900"><div class="absolute -left-16 top-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-center rounded-md h-12 w-12 bg-linear-to-br from-texturepacker-500 to-texturepacker-700 text-white"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 512 512" fill="currentColor" role="img" aria-hidden="true" class="h-6 w-6"><path d="M464 0H144c-26.51 0-48 21.49-48 48v48H48c-26.51 0-48 21.49-48 48v320c0 26.51 21.49 48 48 48h320c26.51 0 48-21.49 48-48v-48h48c26.51 0 48-21.49 48-48V48c0-26.51-21.49-48-48-48zm-80 464c0 8.82-7.18 16-16 16H48c-8.82 0-16-7.18-16-16V144c0-8.82 7.18-16 16-16h48v240c0 26.51 21.49 48 48 48h240v48zm96-96c0 8.82-7.18 16-16 16H144c-8.82 0-16-7.18-16-16V48c0-8.82 7.18-16 16-16h320c8.82 0 16 7.18 16 16v320z"></path></svg></div></div>Alias detection</dt><dd class="mt-2 text-base prose text-gray-600">Sometimes it&#x27;s necessary to use the same sprite multiple times, e.g. in an animation. TexturePacker detects these identical sprites and only adds them to the sprite sheet once. The animation still plays as expected because the animation frames reference the identical sprites.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="mt-10 -mx-4 relative lg:mt-0 lg:col-start-1" aria-hidden="true"><div class="z-10"><figure><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper="" class="gatsby-image-wrapper gatsby-image-wrapper-constrained"><div style="max-width:1248px;display:block"><img alt="" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" src="data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg%20height=&#x27;702&#x27;%20width=&#x27;1248&#x27;%20xmlns=&#x27;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#x27;%20version=&#x27;1.1&#x27;%3E%3C/svg%3E" style="max-width:100%;display:block;position:static"/></div><div aria-hidden="true" data-placeholder-image="" style="opacity:1;transition:opacity 500ms linear;background-color:#080808;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;bottom:0;right:0"></div><picture><source type="image/webp" data-srcset="/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/3af7b/trimming%402x.webp 312w,/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/22358/trimming%402x.webp 624w,/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/adfbb/trimming%402x.webp 1248w" sizes="(min-width: 1248px) 1248px, 100vw"/><img data-gatsby-image-ssr="" data-main-image="" style="opacity:0" sizes="(min-width: 1248px) 1248px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" data-src="/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/2bc71/trimming%402x.png" data-srcset="/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/7f62a/trimming%402x.png 312w,/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/ca21a/trimming%402x.png 624w,/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/2bc71/trimming%402x.png 1248w" alt="Trimming transparency from animation frames to save memory"/></picture><noscript><picture><source type="image/webp" srcSet="/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/3af7b/trimming%402x.webp 312w,/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/22358/trimming%402x.webp 624w,/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/adfbb/trimming%402x.webp 1248w" sizes="(min-width: 1248px) 1248px, 100vw"/><img data-gatsby-image-ssr="" data-main-image="" style="opacity:0" sizes="(min-width: 1248px) 1248px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/2bc71/trimming%402x.png" srcSet="/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/7f62a/trimming%402x.png 312w,/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/ca21a/trimming%402x.png 624w,/static/c3403a3824655c8f6bd62cdafcec9487/2bc71/trimming%402x.png 1248w" alt="Trimming transparency from animation frames to save memory"/></picture></noscript><script type="module">const t="undefined"!=typeof HTMLImageElement&&"loading"in HTMLImageElement.prototype;if(t){const t=document.querySelectorAll("img[data-main-image]");for(let e of t){e.dataset.src&&(e.setAttribute("src",e.dataset.src),e.removeAttribute("data-src")),e.dataset.srcset&&(e.setAttribute("srcset",e.dataset.srcset),e.removeAttribute("data-srcset"));const t=e.parentNode.querySelectorAll("source[data-srcset]");for(let e of t)e.setAttribute("srcset",e.dataset.srcset),e.removeAttribute("data-srcset");e.complete&&(e.style.opacity=1,e.parentNode.parentNode.querySelector("[data-placeholder-image]").style.opacity=0)}}</script></div><figcaption class="text-center text-sm text-gray-700 py-1">Trimmed vs untrimmed sprite sheet:<br/>Save memory and increase performance by removing transparency.</figcaption></figure></div></div></div><div class="lg:grid-cols-2 relative lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-flow-row-dense lg:gap-8 lg:items-center"><div class="relative"><h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl text-gray-900">Pack 